en","ochmoq","och-MOK"],["to close","yopmoq","yop-MOK"],["to say","aytmoq","ayt-MOK"]]},{"id":"school-subjects","title":"School subjects","items":[["maths","matematika","ma-te-ma-ti-KA"],["physics","fizika","fi-zi-KA"],["chemistry","kimyo","kim-YO"],["biology","biologiya","bi-o-lo-gi-YA"],["history","tarix","ta-RIKH"],["geography","geografiya","ge-o-gra-fi-YA"],["literature","adabiyot","a-da-bi-YOT"],["English","ingliz tili","ing-LIZ ti-LEE"],["Uzbek language","o'zbek tili","aw-ZBEK ti-LEE"],["Russian language","rus tili","roos ti-LEE"],["foreign languages","chet tillari","chet til-la-REE"],["art","tasviriy san'at","tas-vi-RIY san-AT"],["music","musiqa","moo-si-KA"],["PE","jismoniy tarbiya","jis-mo-NIY tar-bi-YA"],["computer science","informatika","in-for-ma-ti-KA"],["economics","iqtisodiyot","ik-ti-so-di-YOT"],["law","huquq","khoo-KOOK"],["philosophy","falsafa","fal-sa-FA"],["psychology","psixologiya","psi-kho-lo-gi-YA"],["science","fan","fan"]]},{"id":"classroom","title":"Classroom","items":[["classroom","sinf xonasi","sinf kho-na-SEE"],["desk","parta","par-TA"],["board","doska","dos-KA"],["notebook","daftar","daf-TAR"],["textbook","darslik","dars-LIK"],["homework","uy vazifasi","ooy va-zi-fa-SEE"],["test","test","test"],["grade","baho","ba-HO"],["timetable","dars jadvali","dars jad-va-LEE"],["break","tanaffus","ta-naf-FOOS"],["bell","qo'ng'iroq","kawng-gi-ROK"],["ruler","chizg'ich","chiz-GICH"],["rubber","o'chirg'ich","aw-chir-GICH"],["rucksack","ryukzak","ryook-ZAK"],["dictionary","lug'at","loo-GAT"],["question","savol","sa-VOL"],["answer","javob","ja-VOB"],["mistake","xato","kha-TO"],["pen","ruchka","rooch-KA"],["pencil","qalam","ka-LAM"]]},{"id":"university","title":"University","items":[["university","universitet","oo-ni-ver-si-TET"],["lecture","ma'ruza","ma-roo-ZA"],["professor","professor","pro-FES-sor"],["degree","daraja","da-ra-JA"],["scholarship","stipendiya","sti-pen-di-YA"],["library","kutubxona","koo-toob-kho-NA"],["dormitory","yotoqxona","yo-tok-kho-NA"],["campus","universitet shaharchasi","oo-ni-ver-si-TET sha-har-cha-SEE"],["tuition fees","o'qish to'lovi","aw-KISH taw-lo-VEE"],["semester","semestr","se-MESTR"],["course","kurs","koors"],["essay","insho","in-SHO"],["thesis","dissertatsiya","dis-ser-tat-si-YA"],["diploma","diplom","di-PLOM"],["seminar","seminar","se-mi-NAR"],["entrance exam","kirish imtihoni","ki-RISH im-ti-ho-NEE"],["application","ariza","a-ri-ZA"],["student card","talaba guvohnomasi","ta-la-BA goo-vokh-no-ma-SEE"],["faculty","fakultet","fa-kool-TET"]]},{"id":"school-verbs","title":"School verbs","items":[["to study","o'qimoq","aw-ki-MOK"],["to teach","o'rgatmoq","awr-gat-MOK"],["to ask","so'ramoq","saw-ra-MOK"],["to answer","javob bermoq","ja-VOB ber-MOK"],["to repeat","takrorlamoq","tak-ror-la-MOK"],["to understand","tushunmoq","too-shoon-MOK"],["to remember","eslamoq","es-la-MOK"],["to forget","unutmoq","oo-noot-MOK"],["to explain","tushuntirmoq","too-shoon-tir-MOK"],["to practise","mashq qilmoq","mashk kil-MOK"],["to pass an exam","imtihondan o'tmoq","im-ti-hon-DAN awt-MOK"],["to fail an exam","imtihondan yiqilmoq","im-ti-hon-DAN yi-kil-MOK"],["to write down","yozib olmoq","yo-ZIB ol-MOK"],["to listen","tinglamoq","ting-la-MOK"],["to read aloud","ovoz chiqarib o'qimoq","o-VOZ chi-ka-RIB aw-ki-MOK"],["to think","o'ylamoq","awy-la-MOK"],["to count","sanamoq","sa-na-MOK"],["to spell","harflab aytmoq","harf-LAB ayt-MOK"],["to translate","tarjima qilmoq","tar-ji-MA kil-MOK"],["to graduate","bitirmoq","bi-tir-MOK"]]}],"grammar":[{"id":"pronouns","title":"Pronouns","text":["Uzbek often drops the pronoun, because the verb ending shows who is speaking. Pronouns are for emphasis. There is no he / she difference: \"u\" means both."],"rows":[["I","men","men"],["you (informal)","sen","sen"],["he / she / it","u","oo"],["we","biz","biz"],["you (formal or plural)","siz","siz"],["they","ular","oo-LAR"]],"ex":[["I am a student","men talabaman","men ta-la-ba-MAN"],["you are tall","sen balandsan","sen ba-land-SAN"],["she is my sister","u mening opam","oo me-NING o-PAM"],["we are friends","biz do'stmiz","biz dawst-MIZ"],["they are teachers","ular o'qituvchi","oo-LAR aw-ki-tooy-CHEE"]]},{"id":"singular-and-plural","title":"Singular and plural","text":["Add -lar to the noun. It is the same for every word, so there is no vowel harmony in the plural. After a number, the noun stays singular: ikki kitob (two book)."],"rows":[["kitob (book)","kitoblar","ki-tob-LAR"],["uy (house)","uylar","ooy-LAR"],["bola (child)","bolalar","bo-la-LAR"],["after a number: singular","ikki kitob","ik-KEE ki-TOB"]],"ex":[["one house, houses","bitta uy, uylar","bit-TA ooy ooy-LAR"],["one book, books","bitta kitob, kitoblar","bit-TA ki-TOB ki-tob-LAR"],["one cat, cats","bitta mushuk, mushuklar","bit-TA moo-SHOOK moo-shook-LAR"],["two books","ikkita kitob","ik-ki-TA ki-TOB"],["the children","bolalar","bo-la-LAR"]]},{"id":"to-be-man-san-dir","title":"To be: -man, -san, -(dir)","text":["There is no separate verb \"to be\". Add an ending to the noun or adjective: talaba-man (I am a student). The ending for \"he / she is\" is none, or -dir."],"rows":[["I am","-man","man"],["you are","-san","san"],["he / she is","(no ending) or -dir","dir"],["we are","-miz","miz"],["you are (formal or plural)","-siz","siz"],["they are","-lar","lar"]],"ex":[["I am a student","men talabaman","men ta-la-ba-MAN"],["you are tired","sen charchagansan","sen char-cha-gan-SAN"],["he is a doctor","u shifokor","oo shi-fo-KOR"],["we are happy","biz xursandmiz","biz khoor-sand-MIZ"],["they are at home","ular uyda","oo-LAR ooy-DA"]]},{"id":"bor-and-yo-q-have-there-is","title":"Bor and yo'q: have, there is","text":["Uzbek says \"at me there is\" (bor) or \"at me there is not\" (yo'q). The ending -da means \"at\" or \"in\"."],"rows":[["there is","bor","bor"],["there is not","yo'q","yawk"],["I have","menda ... bor","men-DA bor"],["I do not have","menda ... yo'q","men-DA yawk"]],"ex":[["I have a brother","menda aka bor","men-DA a-KA bor"],["I have a car","menda mashina bor","men-DA ma-shi-NA bor"],["I do not have time","menda vaqt yo'q","men-DA vakt yawk"],["there is a problem","muammo bor","moo-am-MO bor"],["there is no water","suv yo'q","soov yawk"]]},{"id":"present-tense-yapman","title":"Present tense: -yapman","text":["The most common present form: verb stem + -yap + person ending. Bormoq (to go): bor-yap-man. After a consonant it is -ayap, e.g. o'qimoq: o'qiyapman."],"rows":[["I go","boryapman","bor-yap-MAN"],["you go","boryapsan","bor-yap-SAN"],["he / she goes","boryapti","bor-yap-TEE"],["we go","boryapmiz","bor-yap-MIZ"],["you go (formal or plural)","boryapsiz","bor-yap-SIZ"],["they go","boryaptilar","bor-yap-ti-LAR"]],"ex":[["I am eating bread","non yeyapman","non ye-yap-MAN"],["you are reading a book","kitob o'qiyapsan","ki-TOB aw-ki-yap-SAN"],["she works in a bank","u bankda ishlaydi","oo bank-DA ish-lay-DEE"],["we are drinking tea","choy ichyapmiz","choy ich-yap-MIZ"],["they are sleeping","ular uxlayapti","oo-LAR ookh-la-yap-TEE"]]},{"id":"basic-sentences","title":"Basic sentences","text":["The verb goes last. Order: who, where or when, what, verb. Uzbek has no articles: \"kitob\" means \"a book\" or \"the book\"."],"rows":[["I read a book","men kitob o'qiyman","men ki-TOB aw-ki-MAN"],["she drinks tea","u choy ichadi","oo choy i-cha-DEE"],["we go to school","biz maktabga boramiz","biz mak-tab-GA bo-ra-MIZ"]],"ex":[["I read a book","men kitob o'qiyman","men ki-TOB aw-ki-MAN"],["he drinks tea","u choy ichadi","oo choy i-cha-DEE"],["we go to school","biz maktabga boramiz","biz mak-tab-GA bo-ra-MIZ"],["they eat bread","ular non yeydi","oo-LAR non yey-DEE"],["the teacher writes","o'qituvchi yozadi","aw-ki-tooy-CHEE yo-za-DEE"]]},{"id":"negation","title":"Negation","text":["Put -ma- after the verb stem: boraman (I go), bormayman (I do not go). For nouns use \"emas\" (is not): u o'qituvchi emas. \"Yo'q\" means \"there is not\". Always compare with the positive form."],"rows":[["I go","boraman","bo-ra-MAN"],["I do not go","bormayman","bor-may-MAN"],["is","-dir","dir"],["is not","emas","e-MAS"]],"ex":[["I want","men istayman","men is-tay-MAN"],["I do not want","men istamayman","men is-ta-may-MAN"],["I speak English","men inglizcha gapiraman","men ing-liz-CHA ga-pi-ra-MAN"],["I do not speak English","men inglizcha gapirmayman","men ing-liz-CHA ga-pir-may-MAN"],["I like it","menga yoqadi","men-GA yo-ka-DEE"],["I do not like it","menga yoqmaydi","men-GA yok-may-DEE"],["she is here","u shu yerda","oo shoo yer-DA"],["she is not here","u shu yerda emas","oo shoo yer-DA e-MAS"],["I have a car","menda mashina bor","men-DA ma-shi-NA bor"],["I do not have a car","menda mashina yo'q","men-DA ma-shi-NA yawk"],["I understand","tushunaman","too-shoo-na-MAN"],["I do not understand","tushunmayman","too-shoon-may-MAN"],["we are tired","biz charchaganmiz","biz char-cha-gan-MIZ"],["we are not tired","biz charchamaganmiz","biz char-cha-ma-gan-MIZ"],["he works on Sundays","u yakshanba kuni ishlaydi","oo yak-shan-BA koo-NEE ish-lay-DEE"],["he does not work on Sundays","u yakshanba kuni ishlamaydi","oo yak-shan-BA koo-NEE ish-la-may-DEE"]]},{"id":"asking-questions","title":"Asking questions","text":["Add the little word -mi to the end of the sentence. It is the same for every word. Say it with rising voice."],"rows":[["you are a student","siz talabasiz","siz ta-la-ba-SIZ"],["are you a student?","siz talabamisiz?","siz ta-la-ba-mi-SIZ"],["he is here","u shu yerda","oo shoo yer-DA"],["is he here?","u shu yerdami?","oo shoo yer-da-MEE"]],"ex":[["is this your book?","bu sizning kitobingizmi?","boo siz-NING ki-to-bin-giz-MEE"],["are they here?","ular shu yerdami?","oo-LAR shoo yer-da-MEE"],["do you like tea?","choyni yoqtirasizmi?","choy-NI yok-ti-ra-siz-MEE"],["is it cold?","sovuqmi?","so-vook-MEE"],["do you speak English?","inglizcha gapirasizmi?","ing-liz-CHA ga-pi-ra-siz-MEE"]]},{"id":"question-words","title":"Question words","text":["Question words stand where the answer would stand."],"rows":[["what","nima","ni-MA"],["who","kim","kim"],["where","qayer / qayerda","ka-yer"],["when","qachon","ka-CHON"],["why","nega","ne-GA"],["how","qanday","kan-DAY"],["how much","qancha","kan-CHA"],["which","qaysi","kay-SEE"]],"ex":[["what is your name?","ismingiz nima?","is-min-GIZ ni-MA"],["who is he?","u kim?","oo KIM"],["where do you live?","qayerda yashaysiz?","ka-yer-DA ya-shay-SIZ"],["when is the lesson?","dars qachon?","dars ka-CHON"],["why are you late?","nega kechikdingiz?","ne-GA ke-chik-din-GIZ"],["how are you?","qalaysiz?","ka-lay-SIZ"],["how much is it?","qancha turadi?","kan-CHA too-ra-DEE"],["which book?","qaysi kitob?","kay-SEE ki-TOB"]]},{"id":"possessives-and-liking","title":"Possessives and liking","text":["Endings go on the noun: -im (my), -ing (your), -i (his / her). After a vowel: -m, -ng, -si. To say you like something, use \"menga yoqadi\" (to me it is pleasing)."],"rows":[["my book","kitobim","ki-to-BIM"],["your book","kitobing","ki-to-BING"],["his / her book","kitobi","ki-to-BEE"],["our book","kitobimiz","ki-to-bi-MIZ"],["your book (formal)","kitobingiz","ki-to-bin-GIZ"]],"ex":[["my phone","telefonim","te-le-fo-NIM"],["your house (formal)","uyingiz","oo-yin-GIZ"],["his sister","uning singlisi","oo-NING sing-li-SEE"],["I like music","menga musiqa yoqadi","men-GA moo-si-KA yo-ka-DEE"],["I love football","men futbolni yaxshi ko'raman","men foot-bol-NI yakh-SHEE kaw-ra-MAN"]]},{"id":"formal-vs-informal","title":"Formal vs informal","text":["sen (informal): friends, family, children. siz (formal): strangers, older people, work. Verb endings change: -san (informal), -siz (formal)."],"rows":[["how are you?","qalaysan? / qalaysiz?","ka-lay-SAN / ka-lay-SIZ"],["you speak","gapirasan / gapirasiz","ga-pi-ra-SAN / ga-pi-ra-SIZ"],["your name","isming / ismingiz","is-MING / is-min-GIZ"]],"ex":[["how are you? (informal)","qalaysan?","ka-lay-SAN"],["how are you? (formal)","qalaysiz?","ka-lay-SIZ"],["where are you going? (informal)","qayerga borasan?","ka-yer-GA bo-ra-SAN"],["where are you going? (formal)","qayerga borasiz?","ka-yer-GA bo-ra-SIZ"],["please sit down (formal)","o'tiring, iltimos","aw-ti-RING il-ti-MOS"]]},{"id":"past-and-future-simple","title":"Past and future (simple)","text":["Past: -di + person ending (bordim = I went). Future: -aman is the same as the present, with a time word: ertaga boraman (tomorrow I go)."],"rows":[["I went","bordim","bor-DIM"],["you went","bording","bor-DING"],["he went","bordi","bor-DEE"],["we went","bordik","bor-DIK"]],"ex":[["yesterday I was tired","kecha charchagan edim","ke-CHA char-cha-GAN e-DIM"],["I will study tomorrow","ertaga o'qiyman","er-ta-GA aw-ki-MAN"],["we went to the park","biz parkka bordik","biz park-KA bor-DIK"],["I saw him","men uni ko'rdim","men oo-NEE kawr-DIM"],["she wrote a letter","u xat yozdi","oo khat yoz-DEE"]]},{"id":"commands","title":"Commands","text":["Use the bare verb stem for informal and add -ing for formal: kel (come), keling (come, formal). For \"do not\" add -ma: kelma."],"rows":[["come (informal)","kel","kel"],["come (formal)","keling","ke-LING"],["do not come","kelma","kel-MA"],["sit down","o'tiring","aw-ti-RING"]],"ex":[["come here","bu yerga kel","boo yer-GA KEL"],["do not come here","bu yerga kelma","boo yer-GA kel-MA"],["sit down","o'tir","aw-TIR"],["do not sit down","o'tirma","aw-tir-MA"],["be quiet","jim bo'l","jim BAWL"],["do not be late","kechikma","ke-chik-MA"],["open the door","eshikni och","e-shik-NI OCH"],["close the window","derazani yop","de-ra-za-NI YOP"],["listen to me","meni tingla","me-NI ting-LA"],["do not worry","xavotir olma","kha-vo-TIR ol-MA"],["speak slowly","sekin gapir","se-KIN ga-PIR"],["wait a moment","bir daqiqa kut","beer da-ki-KA KOOT"]]},{"id":"can-must-want","title":"Can, must, want","text":["Can: verb + -a olmoq (borolaman, I can go). Must: \"kerak\" (needed). Want: -moqchi + person ending (bormoqchiman, I want to go)."],"rows":[["I can swim","suza olaman","soo-ZA o-la-MAN"],["I cannot swim","suza olmayman","soo-ZA ol-may-MAN"],["I must go","borishim kerak","bo-ri-SHIM ke-RAK"],["I want to go","bormoqchiman","bor-mok-chi-MAN"]],"ex":[["I can swim","men suza olaman","men soo-ZA o-la-MAN"],["I cannot swim","men suza olmayman","men soo-ZA ol-may-MAN"],["can you help me?","menga yordam bera olasizmi?","men-GA yor-DAM be-RA o-la-siz-MEE"],["we must go","bizga ketish kerak","biz-GA ke-TISH ke-RAK"],["we must not go","bizga ketish mumkin emas","biz-GA ke-TISH moom-KIN e-MAS"],["I want to eat","men yemoqchiman","men ye-mok-chi-MAN"],["I do not want to eat","men yemoqchi emasman","men ye-mok-CHEE e-mas-MAN"],["you can come","kelishingiz mumkin","ke-li-shin-GIZ moom-KIN"],["you cannot come","kelishingiz mumkin emas","ke-li-shin-GIZ moom-KIN e-MAS"],["she wants to study","u o'qimoqchi","oo aw-ki-mok-CHEE"],["I must work today","bugun ishlashim kerak","boo-GOON ish-la-SHIM ke-RAK"],["you must not run","yugurish mumkin emas","yoo-goo-RISH moom-KIN e-MAS"]]},{"id":"in-on-at","title":"In, on, at","text":["Uzbek uses endings, not words in front: -da (in, on, at), -ga (to), -dan (from), -ning (of)."],"rows":[["in / on / at","-da","da"],["to","-ga","ga"],["from","-dan","dan"],["of","-ning","ning"]],"ex":[["the book is on the table","kitob stolda","ki-TOB stol-DA"],["the cat is under the table","mushuk stol ostida","moo-SHOOK stol os-ti-DA"],["I am at school","men maktabdaman","men mak-tab-da-MAN"],["I am at home","men uydaman","men ooy-da-MAN"],["the shop is next to the bank","do'kon bankning yonida","daw-KON bank-NING yo-ni-DA"],["the park is near the station","park vokzal yaqinida","park vok-ZAL ya-ki-ni-DA"],["we meet in the morning","ertalab uchrashamiz","er-ta-LAB ooch-ra-sha-MIZ"],["the lesson is at nine","dars soat to'qqizda","dars so-AT taw-kkiz-DA"],["the key is in the bag","kalit sumkada","ka-LIT soom-ka-DA"]]},{"id":"comparing-things","title":"Comparing things","text":["Add -roq to the adjective for \"more\": katta, kattaroq. For \"the most\" put \"eng\" before it: 